X24 in LITE — a wake stamp that outlives its request. runcq, 2026-09-10.
Cluster: 3 x i4i.large, all spot, us-west-1, k8s v1.34.11. Tier-off share on local-path:
the suspend rung needs no bucket (rpoClean gates HIBERNATE, not suspend), so the drill
has no object store, no credential and no IAM between the assertion and the mechanism.

THE PATH, and it needs no race. chert.us/requested-at is the ladder's documented input —
operator-kind-e2e leg 11 says 'whatever wants this share awake stamps it... deliberately
NOT any particular caller's contract'. So a client may stamp a share that is ALREADY UP,
which is what an ensure-live front door does. Nothing clears it: the clear runs on the
TRANSITION into Active and a running share never makes that transition. The stamp ages,
the share suspends carrying it, and decide()'s down-branch read the key's PRESENCE.

  fixed   dilipdalton/flint-lite-operator@sha256:078f4d617b5c7162d327ac2184406fd9804a8f032b3b4e8adda05225e69d1693
  control dilipdalton/flint-lite-operator@sha256:43448615ec4b639c90d552e37aab908c57cddcaf49856d53c61a4fa00dca2eff
Two builds of ONE tree, differing only in idle.rs's down-branch reading and
reconcile.rs's reprovision clear. Every operator pod was drained onto the arm's image
before each run: with two replicas the LEADER is what decides.

